97788083553314,-1.2040065485052764e-05,-0.0004483648226596415,-0.24362406134605408,-0.035678017884492874,0.0,-5.8412379075889476e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0007739647408016026,-0.02332557551562786,-0.07704474776983261,-6.90197994117625e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-9.536738616588991e-07,-5.125868119648658e-05,-0.000760385300964117,0.0,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00018737945356406271,-4.768370445162873e-07,-1.0728830375228426e-06,-0.0021058782003819942,-0.8416036367416382,0.0,-0.00018499570433050394,-0.007648469414561987,0.0,-9.536738616588991e-07,-0.004218251910060644,-3.8265450712060556e-05,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.019382014870643616,-2.2053474822314456e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-8.40390202938579e-05,-3.2186455882765586e-06,-4.6491513785440475e-06,-0.11182434856891632,-0.028464576229453087,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.012914471328258514,0.0,-0.7949394583702087,-0.018593773245811462,-2.50339189733495e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,6774,2268,19582,374,14764,389,264,8866,3579,553,13330,264,43221,504,1817,1372,311,279,17702,1372,29994,65670,504,429,1372,13,220,2938,374,11,55659,525,14764,504,220,16,17,311,220,20,11,504,220,20,311,220,16,15,11,504,220,16,15,311,220,18,11,323,773,389,11,13391,1182,518,220,16,17,13,220,3555,374,279,8381,6629,315,279,9210,518,1817,11936,304,279,6774,2268,19582,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA star-polygon is drawn on a clock face by drawing a chord from each number to the fifth number counted clockwise from that number.  That is, chords are drawn from 12 to 5, from 5 to 10, from 10 to 3, and so on, ending back at 12.  What is the degree measure of the angle at each vertex in the star-polygon?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a18b65768b3723048ce3e1b134203cc188f9702caca5f97f9f6da390cbd952bc"},"seconds":46.644890546798706,"seed":852176301212938192,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, let's follow the steps closely and calculate the degree measure of the angle at each vertex of the star-polygon formed on a clock face.\n\n1. **Understanding the Star-Polygon:**\n   - A clock face has 12 numbers evenly spaced around a circle.\n   - Each number on the clock represents a vertex of the star-polygon.\n   - A chord is drawn from each number to the fifth number counted clockwise from it.\n\n2. **Identify the Chords:**\n   - The chord from 12 to 5\n   - The chord from 5 to 10\n   - The chord from 10 to 3\n   - The chord from 3 to 8\n   - The chord from 8 to 1\n   - The chord from 1 to 6\n   - The chord from 6 to 11\n   - The chord from 11 to 4\n   - The chord from 4 to 9\n   - The chord from 9 to 2\n   - The chord from 2 to 7\n   - The chord from 7 to 12\n\n3. **Calculate the Angle Subtended by Each Chord:**\n   - In a circle, the total angle around the center is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n   - Since there are 12 numbers, each number corresponds to an angle of \\( \\frac{360^\\circ}{12} = 30^\\circ \\).\n   - The chord from 12 to 5 spans 5 numbers, so it subtends an angle of \\(5 \\times 30^\\circ = 150^\\circ\\).\n\n4. **Vertex Angle Calculation:**\n   - The star-polygon is formed by connecting vertices in a specific pattern.\n   - Each vertex in the star-polygon is formed by the intersection of two chords.\n   - The interior angles of the star-polygon can be found by considering the internal geometry of the star.\n   - The star-polygon formed is a regular 12-pointed star (dodecagram), and each vertex angle in such a star can be calculated using the formula for the vertex angles of a regular star polygon with \\( n \\) points and \\( k \\) steps (where \\( k = \\frac{n}{2} + 1 \\) for a star polygon of this type).\n\n   The vertex angle \\( \\theta \\) for a regular star polygon with \\( n \\) points and step \\( k \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = \\frac{(n-4k) \\times 180^\\circ}{n}\n   \\]\n   Here, \\( n = 12 \\) and \\( k = 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\theta = \\frac{(12 - 4 \\times 5) \\times 180^\\circ}{12} = \\frac{(12 - 20) \\times 180^\\circ}{12} = \\frac{-8 \\times 180^\\circ}{12} = \\frac{-1440^\\circ}{12} = -120^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Since we are dealing with an internal angle, we take the positive equivalent:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = 180^\\circ - 120^\\circ = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the degree measure of the angle at each vertex in the star-polygon is \\(\\boxed{60}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{60}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
